From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:05:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: run T8132 sleep exactly as merged
 upstream

Take drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c and sleep-test.c as aurora-silicon/linux
integration/aurora carries them since PR #1314 was merged (head
04f43c7fd9, T8132 brought up on the J713), and drop this tree's own
additions around them: the resume marks and early exception catch in
arch/arm64 (head.S, sleep.S, suspend.c, asm/suspend.h, el2_setup.h),
the ACC_OVRD hook in traps.c, and the measurement switches, probe stub,
wake checks, early arming and AMCC1 stop that sleep.c had grown.

None of those files has changed upstream since the merge, so this is
the team's T8132 sleep path with nothing else in it. The T8132 cache
write-back log in mcc.c goes back to dev_dbg as upstream has it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
